{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>And behold three men.</b> Rashi explained: and Raphael, who healed Abraham, went from there to save Lot. One may ask: what we learned in the chapter about one who hires workers — that the two angels came to Sodom in the evening, and Michael went to save Lot — furthermore, who says it was Michael? If so, he performed two missions: the tidings of Sarah and the salvation of Lot. It appears that there the reading is not Michael but rather Raphael." "<b>Standing.</b> Lingering, as in ונצבת לי. Therefore <b>and he ran toward them</b> — he understood of them that they intended to do some matter."], :book :genesis, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:04:34.115242106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}